cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss H6, please cite this repository."
title: "H6 — Universal Quadratic Image Theorem"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vera
    given-names: Ricardo
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-26
abstract: >-
  A CIEC LAB computer-assisted mathematical result proving that every subset
  H of F_2^12 with cardinality at most 24 is contained in the image of some
  coordinatewise algebraic-degree-at-most-2 map q:F_2^6 -> F_2^12.
  Equivalently, h(6) >= 25. The public artifact includes a human-readable
  proof architecture, exact-kernel witness corpus, adversarial checks and
  a clean-room exact verifier.
keywords:
  - computer-assisted theorem
  - finite geometry
  - coding theory
  - Reed-Muller
  - Boolean functions
  - quadratic maps
  - additive combinatorics
  - reproducible mathematics
  - CIEC LAB
